<title>BELGIUM: EU awards 1,360 T rape oil, soyoil aid contracts.</title>
<headline>EU awards 1,360 T rape oil, soyoil aid contracts.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union awarded contracts for the supply of 1,360 tonnes of rape oil and soyoil to Cuba, Georgia and other countries, the EU Official Journal said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Contracts to supply the 24-member non-governmental organisation Euronaid with 1,170 tonnes of rape oil and 90 tonnes of soyoil were awarded to Belgium's Antwerp-based Cebag at 683.54 and 681.08 Ecus a tonne respectively.</p>
<p>The soyoil is destined for Cuba and the rape oil for unspecified countries.</p>
<p>Another contract was awarded to Antwerp-based Mutual Aid to supply 100 tonnes of rape oil at 942.73 Ecus a tonne.</p>
<p>--Brussels Bureau +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
